index 0000000..b49038c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/full/CAPABILITY-APPROVAL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# Capability approval tokens
+
+claude-guardrails blocks destructive commands. This adds the missing piece: a
+safe way to **approve one** when you actually mean it, without weakening the
+guardrails.
+
+## The problem it solves
+
+Today, to run a blocked command you edit settings or reach for
+`--dangerously-skip-permissions` (which the guardrails also block). And when an
+agent asks "may I run this?", a human running several sessions tends to reflex
+"yes." Both routes are unsafe.
+
+## How it works
+
+A human mints a **one-time, command-scoped, signed token** for an exact command.
+The `approve-gate` PreToolUse hook honors a destructive command only if a valid
+token for that exact command (and working directory) is present. The token is
+consumed on use: one approval, one execution.
+
+The agent **cannot forge a token**: it does not hold the signing key. By default
+the private key is a `0600` file that claude-guardrails' own `Read **/*.key` deny
+rule keeps the agent from reading. For hardware-rooted keys, point
+`CAPABILITY_SIGNER` at a Secure Enclave / Touch ID signer.
+
+## Setup
+
+```bash
+# one time: create the signing key
+claude-guardrails keygen
+```
+
+Wire the hook (alongside the other PreToolUse Bash hooks in your settings):
+
+```json
+{
+  "matcher": "Bash",
+  "hooks": [
+    { "type": "command", "command": "~/.claude/hooks/approve-gate/approve-gate.sh", "timeout": 10 }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+`approve-gate.sh` and `capability-token.sh` install into the same hook directory;
+the hook finds the token CLI next to itself.
+
+## Use
+
+When the agent hits a blocked destructive command, a human approves that exact
+command, from the project directory:
+
+```bash
+claude-guardrails approve "git push --force origin main"
+```
+
+The agent's next attempt at that exact command is allowed once, then the token is
+gone.
+
+## Configuration (env)
+
+| Variable | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `CLAUDE_GUARDRAILS_DIR` | `~/.claude/guardrails` | keys, approvals, audit log |
+| `CLAUDE_GUARDRAILS_TTL` | `300` | token lifetime in seconds |
+| `CAPABILITY_SIGNER` | (unset) | hardware signer override; reads payload on stdin, emits base64 signature |
+
+## Security properties
+
+- **Forgery-resistant.** No signing key, no valid token. The agent has neither.
+- **Command-scoped.** A token for one command does not authorize another, or the
+  same command in a different directory.
+- **Single-use.** Consumed on first match (atomic claim before verify).
+- **Time-boxed.** Expires after the TTL.
+- **Fails closed.** Missing/expired/tampered token, or missing public key, denies.
+  There is no downgrade to unsigned acceptance.
diff --git a/full/approve-gate.sh b/full/approve-gate.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..ba318a6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/full/approve-gate.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# approve-gate.sh — Claude Code PreToolUse hook (matcher: Bash).
+#
+# claude-guardrails hard-blocks destructive commands. This hook adds a safe
+# approval path: a destructive command is allowed only if a human has minted a
+# valid one-time capability token for that EXACT command (see
+# capability-token.sh). No token, expired, tampered, or wrong-key => exit 2.
+#
+# The agent cannot forge a token: it lacks the signing key (protected by the
+# "Read **/*.key" deny rule, or held in a Secure Enclave). A reflexive "yes"
+# is replaced by a cryptographic, command-scoped, single-use approval.
+set -u
+
+SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)"
+TOKEN="${CLAUDE_GUARDRAILS_TOKEN_CLI:-$SCRIPT_DIR/capability-token.sh}"
+
+INPUT="$(cat)"
+# Fail-open on malformed JSON (consistent with scan-commit.sh).
+echo "$INPUT" | jq -e . >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0
+
+CMD="$(echo "$INPUT" | jq -r '.tool_input.command // empty')"
+CWD="$(echo "$INPUT" | jq -r '.cwd // .tool_input.cwd // empty')"
+[ -n "$CMD" ] || exit 0
+
+# Destructive patterns that require an approval token. Mirrors the set
+# claude-guardrails already blocks, made approvable instead of absolute.
+DESTRUCTIVE='(^|[^a-zA-Z0-9_-])rm[[:space:]]+-[a-zA-Z]*[rf]'
+DESTRUCTIVE="$DESTRUCTIVE"'|(^|[^a-zA-Z0-9_-])dd[[:space:]]+'
+DESTRUCTIVE="$DESTRUCTIVE"'|mkfs'
+DESTRUCTIVE="$DESTRUCTIVE"'|(^|[^a-zA-Z0-9_-])git[[:space:]]+reset[[:space:]]+--hard'
+DESTRUCTIVE="$DESTRUCTIVE"'|(^|[^a-zA-Z0-9_-])git[[:space:]]+push[[:space:]].*(--force|-f([[:space:]]|$))'
+DESTRUCTIVE="$DESTRUCTIVE"'|(^|[^a-zA-Z0-9_-])git[[:space:]]+push[[:space:]].*([^a-zA-Z0-9_-])(main|master|production)([^a-zA-Z0-9_-]|$)'
+
+echo "$CMD" | grep -qEi "$DESTRUCTIVE" || exit 0   # not destructive: not our concern
+
+# Destructive: require a valid one-time token for this exact command.
+# A passing check CONSUMES the token (one approval == one execution).
+if [ -x "$TOKEN" ] && "$TOKEN" check "$CMD" "$CWD" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+  exit 0
+fi
+
+{
+  echo "BLOCKED: this destructive command needs a one-time approval token."
+  echo "A human approves THIS exact command, outside the agent, with:"
+  echo "    claude-guardrails approve \"$CMD\""
+  echo "The agent cannot mint it: the signing key is not readable by the agent."
+} >&2
+exit 2
